@startuml delta-write-path
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam component {
  BorderColor #534AB7
  BackgroundColor #EEEDFE
  FontColor #26215C
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #0F6E56
  BackgroundColor #E1F5EE
  FontColor #04342C
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #888780
  BackgroundColor #F1EFE8
  FontColor #2C2C2A
}

title labukDB — Delta Write Path (log/)\nCopyright 2026 Afzal and lakehouse-flight contributors — Apache 2.0

database "Delta table\n(_delta_log/ + Parquet)" as DT #9FE1CB

[TableCreator\n(version 0: protocol + metaData\nonly, no add actions)] as TCR
[ArrowToDeltaSchema\n(Arrow Schema -> schemaString;\nList/Map/Struct all self-similar\nor nested-JSON-object shaped)] as ADS
[ArrowToParquetWriter\n(Arrow -> real Parquet file)] as ATPW

[CommitWriter\n(atomic create-if-absent commit --\noptimistic concurrency, retry on conflict)] as CW
[TableMerger\n(upsert/MERGE by key,\ndataChange=true)] as TMRG
[PartitionRowMerger\n(format-agnostic merge-by-key\nalgorithm -- shared with Iceberg's\nown merger, not duplicated)] as PRM
[Compactor\n(bin-pack small files,\ndataChange=false)] as COMP
[Vacuum\n(delete orphaned files\npast retention window)] as VAC

[LockProvider\n(interface)] as LP
[DynamoDbLockProvider\n(opt-in cross-process lock)] as DDBL
[RemoteWriteSafetyWarning\n(logs on construction of any\nremote, no-lock writer)] as RWSW

TCR --> ADS : build schemaString
TCR --> DT : write version 0

CW --> DT : append add/remove actions
TMRG --> PRM : combineFiles() + merge()
TMRG --> CW : commit via replaceFiles\n(dataChange=true)
COMP --> CW : commit bin-packed files\n(dataChange=false)
VAC --> DT : delete files past\nretired-and-expired
PRM --> ATPW : write new merged\npartition file

CW ..> DDBL : optional, via\nforLocation(location, lockProvider)
CW ..> RWSW : construction --\nwarns if remote + no lock
LP <|.. DDBL

note right of CW
  <b>CONFIRMED BROKEN</b> (real 8-process
  stress test against real MinIO), not
  assumed: remote, no lock -- plain append
  AND TableMerger/Compactor both lose
  commits silently under genuine
  concurrency. MERGE is the WORSE failure
  mode (7 of 8 inserts lost, zero
  exceptions) since its commit unit
  replaces the whole partition, not just
  adds a file.

  Remote, WITH lock (DynamoDbLockProvider):
  <b>done, live-verified</b> -- same failing
  scenarios pass with it engaged.
  TableMerger/Compactor gained their own
  lock-accepting overloads specifically to
  close this (previously only plain
  appendBatch could opt in).

  Local disk: safe unconditionally, lock
  never needed (real atomic filesystem ops).
end note

note bottom of DDBL
  Root cause (not the lock's design, the
  thing it mitigates): S3-compatible
  storage's conditional PUT isn't always
  honored under concurrency the way local
  disk's CREATE_NEW is. DynamoDB's own
  conditional PutItem IS proven atomic
  (8-thread test: 1 success, 7 clean
  conflicts) -- chosen because it mirrors
  real Delta Lake OSS's own
  S3DynamoDBLogStore pattern, not invented.

  Real regression fixed: 8 processes racing
  ensureTableExists() against a brand-new
  lock table all hit ResourceNotFoundException
  then raced createTable -- 6 of 8 got an
  uncaught ResourceInUseException. Fixed by
  catching it and falling through to the
  existing poll-until-ACTIVE loop.
end note

@enduml
